 =?UTF-8?q?=20per-pair=20bucket=20record=20(task=20#23,=20candidate=205.1)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Measured and rejected; reverted in the next commit, kept here so the
numbers in the ledger (iter-143) are reproducible from the branch.

Emit writes a 16 B record (PACK4): half conic x2^10, half tile-local mean,
UNORM16 opacity, UNORM 11/11/10 color, packed with integer-only math
(rec16_codec.h, tested by tests/unit/test_rec16_codec.cpp). The depth key
leaves the record; materialize reads it from the emit's keys layout and
expands each record to the unchanged 32 B slab.

yyzo-bh-07 (p100a), 3 interleaved rounds: 157.23 ms/view vs 167.13 base,
but the same integer packing on the 32 B record gives 154.87 ms/view and
68.68 dB, so the 16 B format itself costs +2.37 ms and 9.3 dB
(hero_vs_ref 59.40; a thin-splat streak from the fp16 conic).
